---
// Chef Line's Journey: the short version of the old game-dev case study.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Project from '../../layouts/Project.astro';
import onion from '../../assets/chef-line-onion.png';
import cover from '../../assets/chef-line.png';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<Project
  title="Chef Line’s Journey"
  summary="A chef ends up in a world made of food and has to fight or cook his way out. Made during my first internship, at game studio Ember Glitch."
  meta="Scrum master and programmer · Feb – Jun 2024 · Team of six · Unity, C#"
  description="A food-themed action adventure made during my internship at Ember Glitch. Scrum master for a team of six, enemy AI with state machines and most of the UI."
>
  <video slot="media" src={`${base}media/chef-line-gameplay.mp4`} poster={onion.src} controls preload="metadata" playsinline>
    <a href={`${base}media/chef-line-gameplay.mp4`}>Watch the gameplay video</a>
  </video>

  <h2>What I did</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Scrum master for two developers and four artists, with mentors from the studio.</li>
    <li>
      Wrote a big part of the 30+ page{' '}
      <a href={`${base}media/chef-line-gdd.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">game design document</a>{' '}
      before we built anything.
    </li>
    <li>Built the enemy AI: idle, roaming, chasing, attacking and fleeing, each as its own state.</li>
    <li>Did most of the UI, the health system and the interactive objects.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why state machines</h2>
  <p>
    My earlier enemies had everything in one script. Splitting each behaviour into its own state made the code
    readable for the other developer, and a new enemy became mostly a matter of reusing states. This is the base
    every enemy runs on:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`public void GoToState(Type type)
{
    _currentState?.Deactivate();

    var next = GetComponentInChildren(type) as State
        ?? new GameObject(type.Name).AddComponent(type) as State;

    next.Machine = this;
    next.Activate();
    _currentState = next;
}`}</code></pre>

  <figure slot="aside">
    <Image src={cover} alt="Cover art of Chef Line’s Journey: the chef surrounded by flying food" widths={[480, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 380px" />
    <figcaption>The game’s cover art.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</Project>
